/*
:name: mod_output_reg_mask_cycle
:type: error
:tolg: 1
:error: lands at cycle\(s\) \(0,0\) but \(1,1\) is declared at the interface
*/

// A mod output reads a plain reg as a feedforward stage only through copies and
// bit slices; through an `&` mask the reg is cycle-0 state. The tree aegraph
// must not respell the mask as a slice (`r#[0..<4]`), which would turn the reg
// into a stage and accept this.
mod top(a:U8) -> (o:U4@[1]) {
  reg r:U8 = 0
  r = a
  o = r & 0xF
}
